  "query_preview": "..\nRHs running around 10-30 percent lower compared to this time\nlast night, however there are still a few valley locations along\nwashes and the Willcox Playa 95-100%. While fog is generally not\nexpected, there could be some brief and localized fog around \nthe Willcox Playa around sunrise. This could exist for clear \nnights like this for awhile given how wet the ground is on the \nplaya. \n\nOtherwise, a beautiful day with highs in the 70s for valley \nlocations and cooler in the mtns. Winds will remain light and \nterrain driven. \n\nThe Friday and early next week systems continue to trend north\nwith less influence to the area. Any showers are now only\nexpected in the White Mtns. A few afternoon breezes will be\npossible Friday and each afternoon, but even that has backed\noff. There is still some uncertainty with early next weekend, \nso we will keep an eye on it. \n\nDaytime highs remain around normal with fluctuations from day \nto day. One thing to note is as we continue to dry out, higher \nvalley locations mid next week could dip to freezing. The past \nseveral nights we have already seen temps 34-39 degrees, so just\nsomething to keep an eye on as we move deeper into the fall. \nPatchy frost will also be possible with some of these locations,\nespecially along washes and water sources.",
